cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bio-ml-eval-protocols — a runnable checklist for honest evaluation of biological ML models"
abstract: >-
  An opinionated, reproducible set of practitioner documents on evaluating
  biological machine-learning models without self-deception: a catalog of
  common methodology traps (homology leakage, random splits on clustered
  data, batch confounders, benchmark redundancy, method/benchmark
  co-development), a vendor-free bootstrap confidence-interval recipe with a
  paired variant for head-to-head comparison, and a preregistration-style
  template for reporting negative results. Ships with `bioeval`, a Python
  package implementing group-aware splitting, split leakage auditing, and
  cluster-aware percentile/BCa and paired bootstrap confidence intervals, so
  the standard is enforced by a dependency rather than asserted in prose.
authors:
